components.lowercase_purl:
The "sbom-checker" mode follows the lowercasing rules used by the sbom-checker.py script (packageurl-python 0.17.6 definitions + the 10 types from sbom_utils.py). Lowercased:
• namespace — for all types except cpan (which requires uppercase), git, huggingface, maven, swid, swift;
• name — for all types except cargo, cocoapods, cpan, cran, git, hackage, huggingface, julia, maven, nuget, opam, rpm, swid, swift, yocto;
• version — only for vscode-extension.
The mode may lowercase case-sensitive identifiers (for example golang, npm, gem).

The "purl-spec" mode uses a snapshot of the official PURL specification as of 2026-11-07. Lowercased:
• namespace — for alpm, apk, bitbucket, brew, composer, deb, github, hex, luarocks, qpkg, rpm, vscode-extension, yocto;
• name — for alpm, apk, bitbucket, bitnami, brew, chrome-extension, composer, deb, github, hex, luarocks, oci, otp, pub, pypi, vscode-extension;
• version — for huggingface, oci, pypi, vscode-extension.
Other types are unchanged; the cpan namespace is unchanged. Some checker warnings (for example, for golang, npm, gem) may remain.

In both modes the rule walks the entire components[] tree, does not touch metadata.component, skips missing, non-string and invalid PURLs, as well as unknown types. Only permitted fields are changed; qualifiers and subpath are preserved verbatim.
